<title>USA: U.S. daily aluminum output dips slightly in April.</title>
<headline>U.S. daily aluminum output dips slightly in April.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Average daily primary aluminum output in the United States dipped slightly to 9,849 tonnes in April, compared to 9,908 tonnes in March and 9,777 tonnes in April 1996, the Aluminum Association said.</p>
<p>Total output in April was 295,479 tonnes, compared to 307,144 tonnes in March, and 293,306 tonnes in April last year.</p>
<p>Output so far this year is 1,185,242 tonnes compared to 1,180,822 tonnes in 1996. The annual rate of production in April was 3,594,995 tonnes compared to 1996 actual output of 3,577,222 tonnes.</p>
<p>((New York Commodity Desk 212-859-1646))</p>
